   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Stretch In\n\nLetters fly in from off-canvas and smear horizontally on the way: a vertex-lag deformation, not a scale.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 2 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A heavy display word needs a fast, physical entrance where the letterforms visibly deform: bars stretch long while stems keep their width.\n- Each letter enters on its own beat and snaps to rest crisp.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The type is small or body-size: the smear reads at display sizes. Use per-character-rise.\n- You want a plain slide-in: use short-slide-right.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"STUDIO\"\n- fill (color): Fill, default \"#ffffff\"\n- font_size (number, 100-700): Font size, default 510\n- entry_stagger (number, 0-12): Entry stagger, default 3\n- travel_frames (number, 4-40): Travel frames, default 33\n- vertex_lag_frames (number, 0-8): Vertex lag, default 3.5\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Stretch In\n\n  Letters fly in from off-canvas and smear horizontally on the way: a vertex-lag deformation, not a scale.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/stretch-in/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"stretch-in\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"2\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    { \"id\": \"text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Text\", \"description\": \"Heavy display word.\", \"default\": \"STUDIO\" },\n    { \"id\": \"fill\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Fill\", \"description\": \"Color of the letters.\", \"default\": \"#ffffff\" },\n    { \"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Type size in px at a 1920×1080 frame.\", \"default\": 510, \"min\": 100, \"max\": 700, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\" },\n    { \"id\": \"entry_stagger\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Entry stagger\", \"description\": \"Frames between letters (30 fps).\", \"default\": 3, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 12, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\" },\n    { \"id\": \"travel_frames\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Travel frames\", \"description\": \"Frames each letter takes to arrive.\", \"default\": 33, \"min\": 4, \"max\": 40, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\" },\n    { \"id\": \"vertex_lag_frames\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Vertex lag\", \"description\": \"Frames the right edge of a letter lags its left edge. More lag, longer smear.\", \"default\": 3.5, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 8, \"step\": 0.1, \"unit\": \"frames\" }\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Stretch In</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Anton&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          font-family: Anton, Impact, sans-serif;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .sti-canvas { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; }\n        .sti-font { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; opacity: 0; font-size: 20px; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"stretch-in\" data-duration=\"2\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"sti-clip\" class=\"clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"2\" data-track-index=\"0\" style=\"position:absolute;inset:0\">\n          <canvas id=\"sti-canvas\" class=\"sti-canvas\"></canvas>\n          <span class=\"sti-font\" aria-hidden=\"true\">STUDIO</span>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, list, fallback) {\n              return list.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            function bz(id, a, b, c, d) {\n              return CustomEase.create(\"sti-\" + id, \"M0,0 C\" + a + \",\" + b + \" \" + c + \",\" + d + \" 1,1\");\n            }\n            // interpolate(frame, [a, b], [from, to], { easing }) as a tween (frames at 30 fps).\n            function tw(tl, el, from, to, a, b, ease, keep) {\n              var t = Object.assign({}, to, { duration: (b - a) / 30, ease: ease || \"none\", immediateRender: !keep });\n              tl.fromTo(el, from, t, a / 30);\n            }\n            // Shrink an element's font size so it fits a fraction of the frame width.\n            function fit(el, size, frac) {\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var maxWidth = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * frac);\n              if (el.scrollWidth > maxWidth) {\n                size = Math.max(12, size * (maxWidth / el.scrollWidth));\n                el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              }\n              return size;\n            }\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2\");\n            function finish(tl) {\n              if (tl.duration() < TOTAL) tl.to({}, { duration: TOTAL - tl.duration() });\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"stretch-in\"] = tl;\n            }\n            // interpolate() with clamping, easing given as a function of progress.\n            function ip(f, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var p = b === a ? 1 : Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (f - a) / (b - a)));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(p) : p);\n            }\n\n            var text = str(vars.text, \"STUDIO\");\n            var fill = str(vars.fill, \"#ffffff\");\n            var W = root.clientWidth, H = root.clientHeight;\n            // The design is a 1920 x 1080 frame, centered and fitted (\"meet\") into the host frame.\n            var s = Math.min(W / 1920, H / 1080);\n            var ox = (W - 1920 * s) / 2, oy = (H - 1080 * s) / 2;\n            var fontSize = num(vars.font_size, 510, 100, 700);\n            var stagger = num(vars.entry_stagger, 3, 0, 12);\n            var travelFrames = num(vars.travel_frames, 33, 4, 40);\n            var lag = num(vars.vertex_lag_frames, 3.5, 0, 8);\n            var TRAVEL = 1500;\n            var px = fontSize * s;\n            var FAMILY = \"Anton, Impact, sans-serif\";\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"sti-canvas\");\n            canvas.width = W;\n            canvas.height = H;\n            var ctx = canvas.getContext(\"2d\");\n            ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false;\n\n            var chars = Array.from(text);\n            var letters = [], srcCanvas = document.createElement(\"canvas\"), srcH = Math.ceil(px * 1.5), base = Math.round(px * 1.1), total = 0;\n            function layout() {\n              var m = document.createElement(\"canvas\").getContext(\"2d\");\n              m.font = px + \"px \" + FAMILY;\n              var x = 0;\n              letters = chars.map(function (ch) {\n                var w = m.measureText(ch).width;\n                var it = { ch: ch, left: x, width: w };\n                x += w;\n                return it;\n              });\n              total = x;\n              srcCanvas.width = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(total) + 2);\n              srcCanvas.height = srcH;\n              var c = srcCanvas.getContext(\"2d\");\n              c.clearRect(0, 0, srcCanvas.width, srcH);\n              c.font = px + \"px \" + FAMILY;\n              c.fillStyle = fill;\n              c.textBaseline = \"alphabetic\";\n              letters.forEach(function (l) { c.fillText(l.ch, l.left, base); });\n            }\n            var ease = bz(\"fly\", 0.2, 0.9, 0.25, 1);\n            var run = Math.max(1, travelFrames - lag);\n            var P = { f: 0 };\n            function draw() {\n              ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);\n              var startX = ox + (1920 * s - total) / 2;\n              // baseline of the 1920 x 1080 design: (height + 0.72 em) / 2\n              var top = oy + ((1080 + fontSize * 0.72) / 2) * s - base;\n              letters.forEach(function (l, i) {\n                var entry = stagger * i;\n                var x0 = null;\n                var w = Math.ceil(l.width);\n                for (var c = 0; c < w; c++) {\n                  var d0 = x0 === null ? dest(c) : x0;\n                  var d1 = dest(c + 1);\n                  x0 = d1;\n                  var a = Math.round(d0), b = Math.round(d1);\n                  if (b <= a) continue;\n                  ctx.drawImage(srcCanvas, l.left + c, 0, 1, srcH, a, top, b - a, srcH);\n                }\n                function dest(c) {\n                  var u = l.width === 0 ? 0 : Math.min(1, Math.max(0, c / l.width));\n                  var rem = ip(P.f, entry + u * lag, entry + u * lag + run, 1, 0, ease);\n                  return startX + l.left + c + TRAVEL * s * rem;\n                }\n              });\n            }\n            layout();\n            draw();\n            function refresh() { layout(); draw(); }\n            if (document.fonts) {\n              document.fonts.load(px + \"px Anton\").then(refresh, function () {});\n              document.fonts.ready.then(refresh, function () {});\n            }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            tl.to(P, { f: TOTAL * 30, duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: draw }, 0);\n            finish(tl);\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
 "sha256": "f483d118f82029fe422911fe3420e0cf03bf2e356382da6ed34de428cf6117cf",
